aker-EV positive (adverse-selection floor stands). Side-finding: B_dir vs RAW price sign is <0.5 / rank-IC<0 -> the maker-profitable side anti-correlates with the price move (crystallized adverse selection). Single seed; maker-EV is the EV-floored metric, AUC/rank-IC/dir-acc are the clean per-model reads.", "params": {"fixed_rounds": true, "fixed_threshold": true, "hp_reuse": true, "seed": 0, "test": [0.68, 1.0], "windows": {"mid_half": [0.1, 0.55], "old_half": [0.0, 0.45], "recent_half": [0.2, 0.65]}}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_recency2.py --symbols ALL --seed 0", "setup": "Recency/drift test v2 (corrected): EQUAL-SIZE large windows (45% of days) sliding old->recent, fixed HP+rounds+per-symbol vol-threshold (reused from main run), same clean test [0.68,1.0). Fixes v1's two flaws (user catch): v1's large windows were START-anchored (volume confounded with recency, never a large RECENT window) and measured B dir-acc cross-config (trained qm=1, eval touch -> ~0.49 noise). v2: windows old_half[0,0.45]/mid_half[0.10,0.55]/recent_half[0.20,0.65]; B measured on its OWN qm=1 config via rank-IC + dir-acc.", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_recency", "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T11:05:00Z"}
{"author": "claude(vm-gce hd2-feats-003)", "cache_id": "gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/maker_labels/{SYM}.npz ; artifacts research_runs/xgb_maker_3mo/{A_{SYM},B_pool}.{json,xgb.json}, preds_{SYM}.npz, MANIFEST.json, SURFACE.json", "commission_loss_pct": 0.02, "commission_win_pct": 0.02, "data_source": "cryptolake", "date_range_end": "2026-05-08", "date_range_start": "2025-05-09", "embargo": "train=last 90 day-indices before val; val [.5525,.65); embargo gap [.65,.68); test [.68,1.0); horizon 60s", "ev_per_trade_pct": null, "experiment_id": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_3mo", "fee_regime": "MAKER_FIRST", "git_commit": "d25b1c4746a7179068949310e63a83950e95d788", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "kind": "strategy", "label_def": "Same label family as xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB; A vol-threshold = p95(|rH60|) on the 90d train window (re-derived); B = maker-better-side on hold-60s/qm1.", "model_family": "xgboost_cascade2_maker_labels", "n_samples": 6902754, "n_trades": 0, "note": "RECENT-90d + Optuna-FROM-SCRATCH vs FULL-HISTORY (head-to-head, same clean test). Mean delta (3mo - full) over 8 syms: A_AUC +0.0028, B oracle dir-acc@10% +0.0016, cascEV@1%(hold/queue) -0.34bp -- ALL within noise. Per-sym A_AUC: BNB .850->.868, BTC .818->.827 (3mo slightly better), DOGE .856->.849, XRP .859->.855 (slightly worse), ETH/LINK/LTC/SOL ~equal. B dir-acc and cascade EV similarly ~equal. CONCLUSION: a model trained on the LAST 90 DAYS with fresh Optuna performs ~THE SAME on the clean test as the full-history (~200d) model -- neither recency+retuning nor extra volume materially changes test performance. => (1) vol-gate A is time-STATIONARY (90d == full, corroborates recency2), (2) direction B ~stationary at this scale, (3) training-data volume SATURATES by ~90 days (older data ~inert: neither helps nor hurts), (4) maker-EV stays NET-NEGATIVE in both (adverse-selection floor unbroken by recency or fresh tuning). Reconciles recency2 (recent-45% mildly > old-45% on B): full-history's predictive content is carried by its recent portion + volume saturation, so full ~= recent-only. Practical: no need to retrain on full history; ~90d suffices; and the maker edge problem is execution (adverse selection), not training-window/tuning. Single seed; thresholds re-derived per window so A operating-point (prec) is not perfectly apples-to-apples, AUC is.", "params": {"optuna_from_scratch": true, "out_sub": "xgb_maker_3mo", "seed": 0, "test": [0.68, 1.0], "threshold_rederived": true, "train_days": 90, "trials": 40, "val": [0.5525, 0.65]}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_makerlabel.py --symbols ALL --trials 40 --seed 0 --train-days 90 --out-sub xgb_maker_3mo ; python3 subs60_xgb_surface.py --symbols BNB BTC DOGE ETH LINK LTC SOL XRP --sub xgb_maker_3mo", "setup": "Train BOTH A+B FROM SCRATCH with Optuna (40 trials) on the LAST 90 day-indices before val (train_days=90, ~3 months), same val [.5525,.65) + clean test [0.68,1.0) as the main run; per-symbol vol-threshold RE-DERIVED on the 90d window (honest from-scratch). Compared head-to-head with the full-history main run xgb-20260531_makerlabels_AB (train [0,.5525), ~200d) on the SAME test. Out-sub xgb_maker_3mo (does not clobber main).", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T11:55:00Z"}
{"author": "claude(vm-gce hd2-feats-003)", "cache_id": "gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/xgb_maker/preds_{SYM}.npz ; result research_runs/xgb_maker/DAILYBUDGET.json", "commission_loss_pct": 0.02, "commission_win_pct": 0.02, "data_source": "cryptolake", "date_range_end": "2026-05-08", "date_range_start": "2025-05-09", "embargo": "test [0.68,1.0) of main run; policy applied on test predictions only; horizon 60s", "ev_per_trade_pct": null, "experiment_id": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_dailybudget", "fee_regime": "MAKER_FIRST", "git_commit": "21f1ebc588391ca635a7099c6a40292e1baca471", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "kind": "strategy", "label_def": "executed NET maker EV(bp) on hold-60s (touch qm0 / queue qm1), B-predicted side, over filled-chosen; per-day single max-(pA-rank x |pB-.5|-rank) window.", "model_family": "xgboost_cascade2_maker_labels", "n_samples": 6902754, "n_trades": 0, "note": "DOUBLE-FILTER (A AND B confidence) + 1 trade/symbol/day. TWO levels: (1) DEPLOY-HONEST (1 trade EVERY day, no test-selection; per-day pick uses only model outputs pA,pB): pooled mean EV -0.77bp touch / -1.27bp queue -- near break-even and a BIG improvement over the A-only top-1% cascade (~-5bp); per-symbol at 1/day touch: LTC +4.7, LINK +3.1, SOL +0.9 positive, ETH -0.4, BTC -1.4, BNB -3.9, DOGE -4.0, XRP -5.1 (WR low 0.34-0.48 -> few big hold-60s tail wins; fill 0.96-1.0). The A-and-B filter + 1-window/day selection lifts per-trade quality far above the A-only cascade. (2) CROSS-DAY SELECTIVITY SWEEP (keep top f% days by combined score) is strongly POSITIVE and monotone -- pooled +4.0 (top50%) / +14.1 (top25%) / +30.9bp (top10%) touch; 6/8 syms rise steeply (LTC +71.7, DOGE +54, LINK +37.9 @top10%) -- BUT this selects the best days ON TEST => SELECTION-OVER-CONDITIONS OPTIMISM (the same failure mode the walk-forward demolished for the cfg/qm/selectivity argmax; n@top10% ~11 trades/sym, high variance). So (2) is PROMISING-BUT-UNCONFIRMED: needs OOS (choose the day-selectivity threshold on val, measure on disjoint test). Minor: pct-ranks normalized over full test (slight look-ahead in cross-day ranking; per-day argmax unaffected). Net read: the double-filter+daily-budget materially improves the deployable maker EV to ~break-even, and the confidence-ranked-days gradient suggests real signal worth an OOS test -- but no positive maker edge is CONFIRMED until that OOS check passes.", "params": {"budget": "1 trade/symbol/day", "cfg": "hold-60s", "cross_day_topf_pct": [100, 50, 25, 10], "policy": "score=pctrank(pA)*pctrank(|pB-0.5|)", "qm": ["touch", "queue"]}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_dailybudget.py --symbols ALL --sub xgb_maker", "setup": "Daily-budget policy on the full-history main-run predictions (OFFLINE, no retrain): combined confidence = pct_rank(pA)*pct_rank(|pB-0.5|) -> requires BOTH A (vol-gate) and B (direction) confident; budget 1 trade/symbol/day = per (symbol,day) take the single max-combined window, trade B's side, executed NET maker EV (hold-60s, touch & queue). Cross-day selectivity sweep keeps top f% of days by combined score.", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T12:25:00Z"}
{"author": "claude(vm-gce hd2-feats-003)", "cache_id": "gs://market-data-0998ac51/research_runs/xgb_maker/preds_{SYM}.npz ; result research_runs/xgb_maker/DAILYGRID.json", "commission_loss_pct": 0.02, "commission_win_pct": 0.02, "data_source": "cryptolake", "date_range_end": "2026-05-08", "date_range_start": "2025-05-09", "embargo": "main-run test [0.68,1.0); policy on test preds only; horizon 60s", "ev_per_trade_pct": null, "experiment_id": "xgb-20260531_makerlabels_dailygrid", "fee_regime": "MAKER_FIRST", "git_commit": "21f1ebc588391ca635a7099c6a40292e1baca471", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "kind": "strategy", "label_def": "executed NET maker EV(bp) hold-60s, B side, over filled-chosen; 1/day = max-|pB-0.5| window among (pA top-qA% AND |pB-0.5| top-qB%).", "model_family": "xgboost_cascade2_maker_labels", "n_samples": 6902754, "n_trades": 0, "note": "EXPLICIT separate A/B confidence windows (strict A AND B), 1 trade/sym/day. POOLED mean EV(bp) over 8 syms, touch (queue near-identical, within ~0.5bp -> robust): grid qA(rows)xqB(cols) 1/2/5/10/25/50% -> qA1%: +23.3/+16.5/+12.2/+20.0/+5.9/+3.3 ; qA2%: +18.8/+12.5/+6.2/+15.3/+3.3/+1.2 ; qA5%: +15.8/+8.3/+3.8/+12.4/-0.2/-1.2 ; qA10%: +13.0/+4.7/+2.1/+9.9/-0.9/-1.0 ; qA20%: +5.2/-0.2/-1.8/-1.1/-2.2/-2.2. KEY: EV rises as BOTH tighten; A-TIGHTNESS IS THE BIGGER LEVER than B-tightness -- e.g. A1%xB10% = +20.0 > A10%xB1% = +13.0 (tightening the VOL gate beats tightening DIRECTION), consistent with A being predictable+stationary while B is the weaker/adverse-selection-bound axis. Max corner A1%xB1% = +23.3bp BUT only ~0.11 trades/day (~13 trades/sym) -> sparse/high-variance. CAVEAT: entire grid is on TEST -> reading the best cell = selection-over-conditions optimism (the failure mode the walk-forward demolished twice); these are MAP coordinates, NOT a confirmed edge. Honest deploy = a FIXED (qA,qB) cell chosen on VAL, measured on disjoint TEST (OOS, pending). Refines _dailybudget (soft product) by making the per-model windows explicit and surfacing the A>>B asymmetry.", "params": {"QA_pct": [1, 2, 5, 10, 20], "QB_pct": [1, 2, 5, 10, 25, 50], "cfg": "hold-60s", "qm": ["touch", "queue"]}, "repro_cmd": "python3 subs60_xgb_dailygrid.py --symbols BNB BTC DOGE ETH LINK LTC SOL XRP --sub xgb_maker --qm touch|queue", "setup": "EXPLICIT 2D confidence-window grid (vs the soft product in _dailybudget): a window qualifies iff pA in top-qA% (vol-gate) AND |pB-0.5| in top-qB% (direction conviction) -- STRICT conjunction; budget 1 trade/symbol/day = highest-B-conviction qualifier per day; executed NET maker EV (hold-60s, touch & queue). OFFLINE on main-run test preds. qA in {1,2,5,10,20}%, qB in {1,2,5,10,25,50}%.", "split_method": "honest_val_test", "status": "exploratory", "supersedes": null, "symbols": ["BNB-USDT-PERP", "BTC-USDT-PERP", "DOGE-USDT-PERP", "ETH-USDT-PERP", "LINK-USDT-PERP", "LTC-USDT-PERP", "SOL-USDT-PERP", "XRP-USDT-PERP"], "ts": "2026-05-31T12:45:00Z"}
